{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"institution":[{"name":"TechRxiv"}],"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2022,4,4]],"date-time":"2022-04-04T08:51:46Z","timestamp":1649062306760},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2021,9,25]]},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers (IEEE)","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2021,9,25]],"date-time":"2021-09-25T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1632528000000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":[],"abstract":"<jats:p>This paper presents a method for automatic generation of a training dataset for a deep convolutional neural network used for playing card detection. The solution allows to skip the time-consuming processes of manual image collecting and labelling recognised objects. The YOLOv4 network trained on the generated dataset achieved an efficiency of 99.8% in the cards detection task.  The proposed method is a part of a project that aims to automate the process of broadcasting duplicate bridge competitions using a vision system and neural networks.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.36227\/techrxiv.16676734","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2021,9,25]],"date-time":"2021-09-25T05:43:15Z","timestamp":1632548595000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Training dataset generation for automatic registration of a duplicate bridge game"],"prefix":"10.36227","author":[{"given":"Piotr","family":"Wzorek","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Tomasz","family":"Kryjak","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"263","container-title":[],"original-title":[],"link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/ndownloader.figshare.com\/files\/30876487","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-applicat